data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":648,"item_id":"fc_0813e6d6447e893d016adb43fd0b0481918395b213e26f5816","output_index":2,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"target_review\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The exercise text and source-context agree with the frozen target after the source context supplies the intended meaning of V(K), the arbitrary admissible lattice M, and L(K). The target preserves all quantifiers: arbitrary prime p, field K of characteristic p, integer lambda with 0 <= lambda < p, and arbitrary admissible lattice M. H001-H004 encode the stated restrictions and module/lattice context; no extra hypothesis such as minimal lattice, p>2, or distinct reduced h-weights is imposed. The conclusion requires both nonzeroness and that every invariant K-subspace is zero or all. The proof's endpoints cover lambda=0 and p=2. The characteristic-zero basis argument uses distinct eigenvalues only over C; the modular argument instead uses matrix units. The argument's comparison of the R-lattice with M tensor K and its claim for arbitrary M are explicitly made rather than restricted to a selected lattice.\",\"locations\":[\"problem.md:3\",\"source-context.md:24-45,47-53\",\"spec.json:/full_target\",\"spec.json:/conclusion\",\"spec.json:/parameters\",\"spec.json:/hypotheses\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/0-4\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/0-7\"]},\"definition_reviews\":{},\"source_reviews\":{},\"structure_review\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The graph has the four frozen H roots and one inference R001 whose output is the unique target P; there are no retained internal, external, or mathlib proposition nodes and no cycles or disconnected proposition branches. The single inference directly cites all four H inputs. Its local facts F001-F003 are produced before their stated uses, and the nonzero-W branch is introduced and discharged in the argument. The displayed proof is globally coherent on the requested structure/AND-closure inspection: the target relies jointly on the original hypotheses and the complete R001 proof, not on alternative paths. No definition prerequisites or source-input application records are applicable. This is not a per-inference packet replay or an automatic structural checker result.\",\"locations\":[\"spec.json:/hypotheses\",\"nl0.json:/propositions\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/inputs\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/output\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/2/produces\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/4/produces\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/5/produces\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/7/discharges\"]},\"findings\":[{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"No global target, definition, source, or graph-closure defect was found in the requested A0-A3/A5 scope. There are no D or M IDs in the exact candidate, so their review maps are empty; signature-evidence.json is empty and no mathlib source review is applicable. Per-inference packet replay is outside this stage as instructed.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/propositions\",\"nl0.json:/inferences\",\"signature-evidence.json:/\"]}]}}"}

